{"id":"g.rw.boundaries.1.afe02bd7c1","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":1,"group":"bnd-intro-81","passage":"<p>During the summer ______ lake's water level drops significantly.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["months: the","months. The","months, the","months; the"],"answer":"C","explanation":"“During the summer months” is an introductory element, not a complete sentence. A <b>comma</b> separates it from the main clause. A semicolon or period would leave the introductory element as a fragment, and a colon must follow a complete independent clause."}
